{"id": "2026-11-21-news-svp-picks-aeschi-and-graber-for-federal-council", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "SVP picks Aeschi and Graber for Federal Council", "summary": "The SVP group nominated Thomas Aeschi and Michael Graber to succeed Guy Parmelin in the 9 December Federal Council election.", "url": "https://www.svp.ch/aktuell/publikationen/medienmitteilungen/bundesratsersatzwahl-svp-fraktion-nominiert-zweier-ticket-mit-thomas-aeschi-und-michael-graber/", "source_domain": "svp.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The SVP parliamentary group nominated National Councillors Thomas Aeschi (Zug) and Michael Graber (Upper Valais) on Friday 20 November as its two candidates to succeed Guy Parmelin in the Federal Council election on Wednesday 9 December. The party's press release says Aeschi was chosen in the sixth round with 37 votes and Graber in the seventh with 42; both will now go before the other parliamentary groups' hearings. Left off were the French-speaking candidates, among them Geneva's Céline Amaudruz, the only woman in the field, and Bernese cantonal minister Pierre Alain Schnegg, along with former party president Marco Chiesa. SVP vice group chair Franz Grüter called it a \"real and good choice\" and reminded the other candidates that they had signed a pledge not to accept election if parliament picked them instead, and that a member elected that way can be expelled under the party's statutes. Criticism came from every other party: SP co-president Cédric Wermuth told SRF it was \"no real choice\", the Greens will skip the hearings, and the Centre's Reto Nause said he could not vote for anyone who had gone after police officers, referring to the pair's 2024 scuffle with federal police in the Federal Palace during a visit by Ukraine's parliament speaker. Both the FDP and the GLP regretted that no candidate from the Latin (French- and Italian-speaking) cantons is on the ticket.", "why": "whoever wins replaces the economy, education and research minister from 1 January. If parliament keeps to the ticket, French-speaking Switzerland drops from two Federal Council seats to one, Elisabeth Baume Schneider's, as Le Temps notes. A \"wild\" election of someone not on the ticket is now openly discussed in the GLP and among the Greens, but the SVP's expulsion rule makes it costly for any SVP member to accept.", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-svp-picks-aeschi-and-graber-for-federal-council", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-12-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SVP", "Thomas Aeschi", "Michael Graber", "Guy Parmelin", "Federal Council"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-r-sti-pitches-swiss-fossil-exit-at-cop31", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Rösti pitches Swiss fossil exit at COP31", "summary": "Albert Rösti presented Switzerland's net-zero law as its fossil-fuel exit plan at COP31 and pledged 10% more for two climate funds.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/cop31-albert-roestis-versprechen-an-der-klimakonferenz", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Federal Councillor Albert Rösti joined about 30 countries' ministers at COP31 in Antalya on Friday 20 November in presenting plans to exit coal, oil and gas, and said Switzerland would raise its contribution to two special climate funds by 10% over four years. Rösti said Switzerland \"already has a plan\": the Climate and Innovation Act that voters approved in 2023, which sets net-zero greenhouse-gas emissions by 2050. He also said Switzerland wants the exit and its timetable written into the conference's final text. SRF points out that, unlike France or Norway, Switzerland presented no year-by-year phase-out schedule, only a summary of targets it had already set, and that around 140 countries have announced net-zero-by-2050 goals. On money, SRF reports that the Federal Council at the same time plans to cut its payment to the overall Global Environment Facility (the multilateral fund the two special funds sit inside), saving almost ten times what the 10% increase adds. Rösti called the increase \"a modest amount\" meant as \"a signal\", and said climate spending was the area least affected by the federal savings package.", "why": "the summit ran into overtime on Saturday over exactly this point, so Switzerland's push for fossil-fuel language is on the record. At home, the headline pledge is smaller than it sounds once the wider fund cut is counted.", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-r-sti-pitches-swiss-fossil-exit-at-cop31", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Albert Rösti", "COP31", "Global Environment Facility"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-youth-strike-fills-swiss-streets", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Youth strike fills Swiss streets", "summary": "Thousands of young people marched in about ten Swiss cities against rearmament and austerity, with clashes in Basel.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/schweizweiter-jugendstreik-jugend-demos-tausende-auf-der-strasse-wenige-zwischenfaelle", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Thousands of school pupils, apprentices and students marched in about ten Swiss cities on Friday 20 November in a \"youth strike\" against rearmament and budget cuts, with organisers claiming 40,000 participants. The alliance behind it lists 13 demands in a manifesto, including a 35-hour week and more holidays for apprentices, three-franc meals at schools and colleges, and putting public money into education, social services and climate protection rather than the military. The Swiss Trade Union Federation backed them and called for a minimum wage of 5,000 francs after an apprenticeship. Most marches were peaceful; Bern cantonal police counted about 2,000 people there. In Basel, after an authorised march, a masked group built barricades and attacked police with fireworks and slingshots, and police used water cannon, rubber bullets and tear gas; two UBS branches were hit with paint. Similar marches took place across Europe, from Prague to London.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-youth-strike-fills-swiss-streets", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Jugendstreik", "Basel", "Swiss Trade Union Federation"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-geneva-jurist-joins-humanitarian-fact-finding-bo", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Geneva jurist joins humanitarian fact-finding body", "summary": "University of Geneva professor Gloria Gaggioli was elected to the International Humanitarian Fact-Finding Commission for 2027-2032.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/amMoELubRdEE", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Gloria Gaggioli, a professor of public international law at the University of Geneva, was elected on Friday 20 November in Bern to the International Humanitarian Fact-Finding Commission for 2027–2032, the foreign ministry said. The commission, set up in 1991 under the First Additional Protocol to the Geneva Conventions, is the only permanent treaty body for investigating alleged violations of the laws of war, but it can act only when the states involved accept it. Switzerland backed her candidacy.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-geneva-jurist-joins-humanitarian-fact-finding-bo", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Gloria Gaggioli", "International Humanitarian Fact-Finding Commission"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-killer-robot-talks-end-without-a-ban", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Killer-robot talks end without a ban", "summary": "CCW states in Geneva agreed to elaborate an instrument on lethal autonomous weapons over two years but not to negotiate a binding ban.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/21/nations-agree-to-draft-rules-for-killer-robots-at-arms-control-summit", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The 128 member states of the UN Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons (CCW) agreed in Geneva early on Saturday 21 November to \"elaborate\" an international instrument on lethal autonomous weapons, often called \"killer robots\", over the next two years, but not to negotiate a legally binding ban. Nearly 100 countries had pushed for treaty negotiations on weapons that can kill without a human making the final decision to fire. The United States, Russia and Israel were among those opposed, and since CCW decisions need consensus, any one of them could block. Talks on the wording ran through the night, and the conference's Swiss chair said some states had rejected the word \"negotiate\". He called the result proof that \"multilateral diplomacy can still deliver concrete results\". The Stop Killer Robots coalition called the mandate \"watered down\", and Human Rights Watch called the outcome disappointing.", "why": "after more than ten years of talks, this is the first mandate to draft actual rules, but \"elaborate\" is weaker than \"negotiate\", and the states building these weapons kept their veto. Campaigners say AI-targeting systems are already in use in current wars.", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-killer-robot-talks-end-without-a-ban", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["CCW", "United States", "Russia", "Israel", "Stop Killer Robots"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-two-tankers-hit-off-oman-after-hormuz", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Two tankers hit off Oman after Hormuz", "summary": "Two tankers were struck by unidentified projectiles off Khasab after leaving the Strait of Hormuz, and the IRGC claimed two US drone kills.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/monde/moyenorient/deux-petroliers-frappes-par-des-projectiles-d-origine-inconnue-en-sortant-du-detroit-d-ormuz", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Two tankers were hit by \"projectiles of unknown origin\" on Saturday 21 November off Khasab, Oman, just after leaving the Strait of Hormuz, the UK military's maritime agency UKMTO reported; no injuries were reported. One ship was hit at the stern and the other in its engine room. The same day, Iran's Revolutionary Guards (IRGC) said, via state broadcaster IRIB, that they had shot down a US MQ-9 drone with a new air-defence system, and later an MQ-1 over Qeshm island. The US military had not commented. Iran's foreign minister Abbas Araghchi said on Friday that Iran's seven conditions, including an end to the war and the lifting of sanctions and the US naval blockade of its ports, \"must be implemented for the Strait of Hormuz to reopen\", though he called the timetable \"flexible\". Donald Trump said Tehran \"want[s] to make a deal\" but not one he could accept.", "why": "before the US–Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February, a fifth of the world's oil and liquefied gas passed through Hormuz. Continued attacks keep shipping insurance and energy prices high while talks stay stuck.", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-two-tankers-hit-off-oman-after-hormuz", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "Strait of Hormuz", "IRGC", "UKMTO", "Oman"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-vetoes-stall-grynspan-s-bid-for-un-chief", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Vetoes stall Grynspan's bid for UN chief", "summary": "Rebeca Grynspan led the ninth Security Council straw poll for Secretary-General but two permanent members discouraged her.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/monde/la-costaricaine-rebeca-grynspan-en-tete-pour-diriger-l-onu-mais-deux-veto-des-grandes-puissances-bloquent-sa-nomination", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Costa Rica's Rebeca Grynspan again topped the UN Security Council's informal vote on the next Secretary-General on Friday 20 November, but two \"discourage\" votes from permanent members still block her, Le Temps reports. In the ninth such straw poll, she had ten \"encourage\" votes, four \"discourage\" and one abstention; colour-coded ballots showed three of the five permanent members in favour and two against. Argentina's Rafael Grossi, head of the International Atomic Energy Agency, came second with eight in favour and six against, three of them from permanent members, and the UAE's Lana Nusseibeh got seven in favour. The ballots are anonymous, so which permanent members objected is not public. António Guterres's term ends on 31 December, about forty days away.", "why": "without a nominee the UN could have no confirmed chief on 1 January, with knock-on effects in Geneva, where many of its agencies face budget cuts.", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-vetoes-stall-grynspan-s-bid-for-un-chief", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Rebeca Grynspan", "UN Security Council", "Rafael Grossi", "António Guterres"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-gupta-jailed-for-pannun-murder-plot", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Gupta jailed for Pannun murder plot", "summary": "A US judge sentenced Nikhil Gupta to 19 years and seven months for plotting to kill Sikh separatist Gurpatwant Singh Pannun.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-judge-jails-indian-national-in-foiled-sikh-separatist-murder-plot/live-80008104", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A US federal judge in New York sentenced Indian national Nikhil Gupta on Friday 20 November to 19 years and seven months in prison for plotting to have Sikh separatist leader Gurpatwant Singh Pannun killed. Gupta, 55, pleaded guilty in February to murder-for-hire, conspiracy and money laundering. He paid $15,000 to a man he thought was a hitman but who was an undercover US agent. Prosecutors say an Indian government employee recruited him in 2023 and remains abroad, outside US custody. India denies any involvement and has designated Pannun, who leads the Khalistan separatist group Sikhs for Justice, a terrorist. Judge Victor Marrero said Gupta faces deportation to India after his sentence. US prosecutors had sought nearly 24 years.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-gupta-jailed-for-pannun-murder-plot", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Nikhil Gupta", "Gurpatwant Singh Pannun", "India", "Sikhs for Justice"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-french-officers-jailed-for-zecler-beating", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "French officers jailed for Zecler beating", "summary": "A Paris court sentenced three officers for the racist 2020 beating of music producer Michel Zecler.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/21/three-french-police-officers-sentenced-over-racist-assault-on-black-man", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A Paris criminal court sentenced three police officers on Friday 20 November for the racist beating of Black music producer Michel Zecler at his studio in November 2020, a rare conviction for police violence in France. Aurélien Lapersonne and Philippe Tondeux each got five years, of which two and one and a half years respectively must be served; Pierre Plantier got five years with four suspended, the remaining year to be served with an electronic tag. The court found racism to be an aggravating factor and said the officers' falsified report damaged their credibility. Zecler's own security cameras filmed the attack.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-french-officers-jailed-for-zecler-beating", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Michel Zecler", "France"]}
{"id": "2026-11-21-news-russian-strikes-kill-two-in-kryvyi-rih", "date": "2026-11-21", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian strikes kill two in Kryvyi Rih", "summary": "Russian missile and drone strikes on Kryvyi Rih killed two and injured 47, local officials said.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/11/21/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-deux-morts-et-47-blesses-dans-des-frappes-russes-sur-kryvy-rih-ville-natale-de-volodymyr-zelensky_6810982_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Russian strikes on Kryvyi Rih, Volodymyr Zelensky's home city, on Friday evening 20 November killed a 7-year-old boy and a 20-year-old nurse and injured 47, according to local officials. The head of the city's defence council said two ballistic missiles hit a residential area in the centre, and drones struck again while rescuers were at work; 23 apartment buildings, a hospital and schools were damaged. Overnight, Russia launched three ballistic missiles and 148 drones across Ukraine, of which 117 drones were shot down or jammed, Ukraine's air force said.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-21-news-russian-strikes-kill-two-in-kryvyi-rih", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-21", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kryvyi Rih"]}
